 ### SS-NeRF
-SS-NeRF employs an encoding function and two position decoding functions (one direction-dependent, one direction-independent) represented by MLPs to produce various scene properties [S1, 10636-specific-loss-formulations.md]. It is trained to produce color, semantic labels, surface normal, shading, keypoints, and edges using a combination of losses: MSE for color and surface normals; MAE for shading, keypoints and edges; and cross-entropy for semantic labels [S1, 10636-specific-loss-formulations.md]. Choose SS-NeRF when multi-task scene property synthesis is required alongside view synthesis [S1, 10636-specific-loss-formulations.md].
